"_idioma" = "English";
"AYUDA" = "fotos-iphone — copies photos and videos from the iPhone to the Mac over USB, as original files.\n\nUSAGE\n  fotos-iphone                    (assistant: asks what to copy)\n  fotos-iphone --profile Trip --from 2026-10-01 --to 2026-10-15 --dest ~/Pictures/Trip\n  fotos-iphone --from 2026-01-01 --to 2026-01-31 --dest ~/Pictures/MyBackup [--simulate]\n  fotos-iphone --list album.txt --dest ~/Pictures/Trip [--simulate]\n  fotos-iphone --inspect [--last 30 | --number 1234 --number 1235 | --name THQV8599]\n\nOPTIONS\n  --from YYYY-MM-DD  Copy what was taken from that day (included).\n  --to YYYY-MM-DD    …up to that day (included). Used instead of --list.\n  --days N           The last N days (today included).\n  --last-month       The whole previous month (from the 1st to the last day).\n  --all              The whole iPhone.\n  --list PATH        Album list created by the Shortcut\n                     (one line per item: IMG_1234|2026-10-20T14:33:12).\n  --dest PATH        Folder where the files and informe.csv (the report) are saved.\n  --simulate         Shows what would be copied and what would be skipped, without copying.\n  --delete           Deletes from the iPhone what is fully backed up in --dest (original and\n                     edited), then checks on the iPhone that it was deleted. Asks you to type\n                     a key; with --simulate it only shows what it would delete.\n  --report PATH      With --delete: the candidates come from a copy's informe.csv\n                     (the backup is its folder, unless --dest is given).\n  --sha256           Adds the SHA-256 fingerprint of each copied file to the report.\n  --inspect          Shows how the Mac sees the iPhone's files (names, groups, source, camera).\n  --cameras          Counts items by camera and source (in the period, or on the whole iPhone).\n  --dump             Saves every file the iPhone shows to catalogo-iphone.csv (diagnostics).\n  --last N           With --inspect: the N most recent items (30 by default).\n  --number N         Only item IMG_N (or WIOR2185…) when inspecting, copying or deleting.\n                     It is copied whatever its source. Can be repeated.\n  --name NAME        Only the file from another app with that name (e.g. THQV8599). Can be repeated.\n  --yes              Copies without asking (by default it simulates and asks for confirmation).\n  --language CODE    Language of the messages: es, en (default: the system's).\n  --help             Shows this help.\n\nASSISTANT AND PROFILES\n  (no options)       Assistant: asks what to copy, step by step, and simulates before copying.\n  --wizard           The same.\n  --profile NAME     Uses a profile's options (other options modify it).\n  --save-profile NAME  Saves the given options as a profile.\n  --profiles         Shows the available profiles.\n  --delete-profile NAME  Deletes a saved profile (built-in ones can't be deleted).\n\nWHAT TO COPY (default: photos and videos from this iPhone's camera, original + edited)\n  --sources LIST     camera, screenshots, recordings, apps (comma-separated) or all.\n  --this-iphone      Only this iPhone's camera, worked out from its recent photos (default).\n  --model NAME       Accepted camera model. Can be repeated.\n  --any-camera       Accepts photos and videos from any camera.\n  --versions V       originals (original only) · final (the edited one if it exists)\n                     · both (original + edited).\n  --no-aae           Without the edit instructions (.AAE).\n  --no-videos        Without videos.\n  --max-video SIZE   Skips videos larger than SIZE (e.g. 2GB, 500MB).\n  --live-videos      Includes the Live Photo videos.\n  --raw MODE         include · exclude · only (RAW/DNG photos only).\n  --layout MODE      flat (all together) · month (2026/2026-10/) · day (2026/2026-10/2026-10-20/).\n\n  Every option is also accepted in Spanish (--desde, --hasta, --destino, --simular…).\n\nBEFORE YOU START\n  · iPhone: Settings → Apps → Photos → Transfer to Mac or PC → “Keep Originals”.\n  · iPhone unlocked and connected by cable; Image Capture open and Photos closed on the Mac.";

